      "about.eyebrow":"About","about.title":"About Amira",
      "about.body":"Amira Khalid is a professional makeup artist based in Jeddah, passionate about enhancing your natural beauty with an elegant artistic touch fit for your special occasions — from your wedding day to your finest evenings out. Amira uses professional international brands and follows the highest hygiene standards with dedicated tools for every client.",
      "about.story":"<p>Hello, I’m Amira.</p><p>My love for makeup started at a young age, long before I imagined it could ever become my profession.</p><p>I loved doing my own makeup, then my family’s and my friends’, and over time I discovered that what draws me to makeup most isn’t the colors or the products — it’s how, with small details, you can see the same face… only more beautiful.</p><p>My own experiences with makeup shaped the way I work with my clients today. Sometimes I would have my makeup done by an artist and it would be beautiful, but I wouldn’t feel that it looked like me, or reflected the way I like to see myself.</p><p>Perhaps that’s where a conviction began that I still carry today: <strong>before I begin, I like to listen to you.</strong></p><p>I like to know how you like to see yourself, what you love and what doesn’t feel like you. Then my role and my experience come in; I suggest what I see as most beautiful for your features, explain my thinking, and together we reach a result that brings your taste and my touch together.</p><p>In 2016, that love became my profession — and one of the most beautiful things this work has given me is my clients.</p><p>To this day I feel genuine joy with every bride who comes to me, and every client who chooses me for her occasion. I deeply appreciate that she has many options, and still she saw my work, chose me, and trusted me. To me that trust has never become ordinary.</p><p>One of the things that makes me happiest in my work is hearing a client say:</p><p class=\"about-quote\">“This is the first time I’ve had my makeup done and felt that this is me.”</p><p>To me, that sentence sums up a great deal. Because my goal isn’t to change you or make you see a different person in the mirror. My goal is for makeup to bring out your beauty in the way you like to see yourself.</p><p>I don’t want to impose an image I find beautiful if you don’t see yourself in it. I want to bring together my experience and my touch with your beauty and your taste, so the result is beautiful on you and still looks like you.</p><p>Whether you’re a bride or have an occasion coming up, I genuinely am glad you’re here, I appreciate your choice and your trust, and I always hope to be worthy of it. 🤍</p>",
      "about.ch1":"The Beginning",
      "about.storyPart1":"<p class=\"story-lead\">Hello, I’m Amira.</p><p>My love for makeup started at a young age, long before I imagined it could ever become my profession.</p><p>I loved doing my own makeup, then my family’s and my friends’, and over time I discovered that what draws me to makeup most isn’t the colors or the products — it’s how, with small details, you can see the same face… only more beautiful.</p><p>My own experiences with makeup shaped the way I work with my clients today. Sometimes I would have my makeup done by an artist and it would be beautiful, but I wouldn’t feel that it looked like me, or reflected the way I like to see myself.</p>",
      "about.belief":"Before I begin, I like to listen to you.",
      "about.beliefSub":"I like to know how you like to see yourself, what you love and what doesn’t feel like you. Then my role and my experience come in; I suggest what I see as most beautiful for your features, explain my thinking, and together we reach a result that brings your taste and my touch together.",
      "about.ch2":"The Craft",
      "about.storyPart2":"<p>In 2016, that love became my profession — and one of the most beautiful things this work has given me is my clients.</p><p>To this day I feel genuine joy with every bride who comes to me, and every client who chooses me for her occasion. I deeply appreciate that she has many options, and still she saw my work, chose me, and trusted me. To me that trust has never become ordinary.</p><p>One of the things that makes me happiest in my work is hearing a client say:</p>",
      "about.clientQuote":"“This is the first time I’ve had my makeup done and felt that this is me.”",
      "about.storyPart3":"<p>To me, that sentence sums up a great deal. Because my goal isn’t to change you or make you see a different person in the mirror. My goal is for makeup to bring out your beauty in the way you like to see yourself.</p><p>I don’t want to impose an image I find beautiful if you don’t see yourself in it. I want to bring together my experience and my touch with your beauty and your taste, so the result is beautiful on you and still looks like you.</p><p>Whether you’re a bride or have an occasion coming up, I genuinely am glad you’re here, I appreciate your choice and your trust, and I always hope to be worthy of it. 🤍</p>",
      "about.teaser":"<p>Hello, I’m Amira.</p><p>My love for makeup started at a young age, long before I imagined it could ever become my profession.</p><p>Over time I discovered that what draws me to makeup most isn’t the colors or the products — it’s how, with small details, you can see the same face… only more beautiful.</p><p>Perhaps that’s where a conviction began that I still carry today: <strong>before I begin, I like to listen to you.</strong></p><p>My goal isn’t to change you or make you see a different person in the mirror. My goal is for makeup to bring out your beauty in the way you like to see yourself.</p>",
      "about.readStory":"Read My Full Story",
      "about.joinDay":"If you’d like me to be part of your day",
      "philosophy.title":"My Philosophy — The Beauty of Remaining You",
      "philosophy.body":"<p>I believe bridal makeup should preserve and enhance the beauty of who you are at this moment in your life.</p><p>You are a bride, and there is a natural softness and beauty in your features that I never want makeup to overpower or replace.</p><p>My approach is not to change your features or create a different face. It is to understand your face, enhance what is already beautiful, create balance between your features, and bring everything together in a way that still feels completely like you.</p><p>I don’t want your wedding makeup to be defined by a passing trend or by heavy techniques that change the way you naturally look. I want the beauty we create together on your wedding day to remain beautiful in your photographs for many years to come.</p><p>When you look back at your wedding photographs twenty, thirty, or even forty years from now, I want you to see yourself as you truly were on that special day — a beautiful bride whose natural features were enhanced, not changed.</p><p>I want you to remember your beauty, your expression, and how you felt, rather than looking at the photograph and only noticing a makeup trend that belonged to a certain time.</p><p>That is what beautiful bridal makeup means to me: makeup that enhances your beauty today while preserving your identity for the memories you will keep for a lifetime.</p><p class=\"philosophy-closing\">Not a different face. Not a passing trend.<br>Just you — today, and for all the years to come.</p>",
